module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.QuasicoherentAlgebras
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Local generation and finite type for the symmetric and exterior powers

Let `(X, 𝒪_X)` be a ringed space and `F` a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules. This file proves clauses (1)
and (2) of Stacks Tag 01CK for the **symmetric** and the **exterior** powers: if `F` is locally
generated by sections then so is each `Symⁿ F` and each `⋀ⁿ F`, and if `F` is of finite type then
so is each of them. The tensor third of the two clauses is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localGeneratorsData_tensorPower` and `isFiniteType_tensorPower`
of `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorPowerLocalGenerators`.

Both clauses come from one construction, and it needs strictly less than Tag 01CJ does: only the
**surjectivity** half of that lemma, which carries no exactness hypothesis. A family of sections
generating a sheaf of modules `M` is an epimorphism `p : free I ⟶ M`, and

* `SheafOfModules.SymPresentation.epi_symDesc_app` and
  `SheafOfModules.ExtPresentation.epi_extDesc_app` say that `Symⁿ(p)` and `⋀ⁿ(p)` are again
  epimorphisms, in every degree;
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerFreeIsoAnyIndex` and `exteriorPowerFreeIsoAnyIndex`
  identify `Symⁿ(free I)` with `free {d : I →₀ ℕ | d.degree = n}` and `⋀ⁿ(free I)` with
  `free (powersetCard I n)`, with **no finiteness hypothesis** on `I`.

Composing gives an epimorphism onto `Symⁿ M`, respectively `⋀ⁿ M`, from a free sheaf of modules
on an index type which is finite as soon as `I` is — and that single implication is what makes
the construction serve clause (2) as well as clause (1).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.freePowerAlgebras`: the chosen package of algebras of a free sheaf of
  modules.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfOpenSubspaceIso`: generating sections transported
  from the open subspace `U` back to the slice site over `U`. This is the analogue for generating
  sections of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationOfOpenSubspaceIso`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_epi_free_symmetricPower` and `exists_epi_free_exteriorPower`: the
  construction described above.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower_over` and
  `exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower_over`: **generating sections of `F` over an open give
  generating sections of every symmetric, respectively exterior, power of `F` over that same
  open**, finitely many when the given ones are finitely many.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localGeneratorsData_symmetricPower` and
  `nonempty_localGeneratorsData_exteriorPower`: **clause (1) of Tag 01CK** for the symmetric and
  the exterior powers.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_symmetricPower` and `isFiniteType_exteriorPower'`:
  **clause (2) of Tag 01CK** for the symmetric and the exterior powers.

## Implementation notes

**Why the open subspace has to be crossed.** The surjectivity half of Tag 01CJ is proved on
stalks, so it is available over a *topological space* and not over an arbitrary site; the slice
site `(Opens X, J.over U)` is not of that form. The passage is the one
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_symmetricPower_over` already makes — the equivalence
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.openSubspaceEquiv` between sheaves of modules on the slice site and on the
open subspace, followed by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerOverIso` — with
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfOpenSubspaceIso` in place of
`presentationOfOpenSubspaceIso`. For the tensor powers no such crossing is needed, which is why
they are in a separate file.

**Nothing is narrowed, and the existing finite-type statement is not this clause.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_exteriorPower` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorPowerFiniteType` assumes `F` of **finite
presentation**, which is strictly stronger than clause (2)'s hypothesis; it is deliberately not
tagged there. The statement below, `isFiniteType_exteriorPower'`, assumes only finite type and is
the clause. Both are kept: the first is what Tag 0B3T consumes together with quasi-coherence.

**Every index type is finite as soon as the given one is**, and in both cases the implication is
`inferInstance`: `{d : I →₀ ℕ | d.degree = n}` is a subtype of a finitely supported function type
on a finite domain, and `Set.powersetCard I n` is a subtype of `Set I`. The decidable equality
the monomial basis needs and the linear order Mathlib's exterior basis needs are supplied
classically, so neither appears in a statement.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CK)
* [Stacks Project, Section 17.21](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CF)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf AlgebraicGeometry
  TopologicalSpace RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### The powers of a sheaf of modules generated by sections -/

section Global

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- The chosen package of tensor, exterior and symmetric algebras of the free sheaf of modules on
an index type. This is `SheafOfModules.algebras` at the site of opens of a space; it is an
`abbrev` so that the two spellings of the structure sheaf as a sheaf of rings are crossed at
reducible transparency. -/
noncomputable abbrev freePowerAlgebras (Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
      CommRingCat.{u}) (I : Type u) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.free
        (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) I) :=
  _root_.SheafOfModules.algebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X)
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) I)

variable {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp)}

/-- An epimorphism out of a sheaf of modules isomorphic to a free one gives an epimorphism from a
free sheaf of modules, with finite index type whenever the free sheaf is on a finite one. -/
private theorem exists_epi_free_of_iso_epi {I K : Type u}
    {T : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp)}
    (e : T ≅ _root_.SheafOfModules.free
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) K) (f : T ⟶ M) [Epi f]
    (hK : Finite I → Finite K) :
    ∃ (K : Type u) (g : _root_.SheafOfModules.free
        (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) K ⟶ M),
      Epi g ∧ (Finite I → Finite K) :=
  ⟨K, e.inv ≫ f, inferInstance, hK⟩

/-- **An epimorphism onto `M` from a free sheaf of modules induces one onto every symmetric power
of `M`**, from the free sheaf of modules on the degree-`n` multidegrees in the given index type.
The two inputs are the surjectivity half of Tag 01CJ,
`SheafOfModules.SymPresentation.epi_symDesc_app`, and the computation of the symmetric power of a
free sheaf of modules on an arbitrary index type,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricPowerFreeIsoAnyIndex`. -/
theorem exists_epi_free_symmetricPower (I : Type u)
    {p : _root_.SheafOfModules.free
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) I ⟶ M} (hp : Epi p)
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) M) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (K : Type u) (g : _root_.SheafOfModules.free
        (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) K ⟶ A.symmetricPower n),
      Epi g ∧ (Finite I → Finite K) := by
  classical
  have := hp
  have := _root_.SheafOfModules.SymPresentation.epi_symDesc_app
    (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).symmetricGenerator A.symmetricGenerator
    (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra
    A.symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra p n
  exact exists_epi_free_of_iso_epi (K := {d : I →₀ ℕ | d.degree = n})
    (symmetricPowerFreeIsoAnyIndex (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) I n
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I))
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.SymPresentation.symDesc
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).symmetricGenerator A.symmetricGenerator
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra
      A.symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra p).app (n : ℤ)) fun _ => inferInstance

/-- **An epimorphism onto `M` from a free sheaf of modules induces one onto every exterior power
of `M`**, from the free sheaf of modules on the `n`-element subsets of the given index type. The
exterior half of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_epi_free_symmetricPower`; the linear order
Mathlib's exterior basis needs is supplied by well-ordering the index type. -/
theorem exists_epi_free_exteriorPower (I : Type u)
    {p : _root_.SheafOfModules.free
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) I ⟶ M} (hp : Epi p)
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) M) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ (K : Type u) (g : _root_.SheafOfModules.free
        (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) Osharp) K ⟶ A.exteriorPower n),
      Epi g ∧ (Finite I → Finite K) := by
  classical
  have := hp
  let _ : LinearOrder I := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  have := _root_.SheafOfModules.ExtPresentation.epi_extDesc_app
    (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).exteriorGenerator A.exteriorGenerator
    (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).exterior_isExteriorAlgebra
    A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra p n
  exact exists_epi_free_of_iso_epi (K := Set.powersetCard I n)
    (exteriorPowerFreeIsoAnyIndex (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) I n
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I))
    ((_root_.SheafOfModules.ExtPresentation.extDesc
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).exteriorGenerator A.exteriorGenerator
      (freePowerAlgebras Osharp I).exterior_isExteriorAlgebra
      A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra p).app (n : ℤ)) fun _ => inferInstance

/-- **Generating sections of `M` give generating sections of every symmetric power of `M`**,
finitely many when the given ones are finitely many. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower (σ : M.GeneratingSections)
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) M) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ τ : (A.symmetricPower n).GeneratingSections, (Finite σ.I → Finite τ.I) := by
  obtain ⟨K, g, hg, hK⟩ := exists_epi_free_symmetricPower σ.I (p := σ.π) inferInstance A n
  have := hg
  exact ⟨(_root_.SheafOfModules.free.generatingSections K).ofEpi g, hK⟩

/-- **Generating sections of `M` give generating sections of every exterior power of `M`**,
finitely many when the given ones are finitely many. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower (σ : M.GeneratingSections)
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥X) M) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ τ : (A.exteriorPower n).GeneratingSections, (Finite σ.I → Finite τ.I) := by
  obtain ⟨K, g, hg, hK⟩ := exists_epi_free_exteriorPower σ.I (p := σ.π) inferInstance A n
  have := hg
  exact ⟨(_root_.SheafOfModules.free.generatingSections K).ofEpi g, hK⟩

end Global

/-! ### The same over an open -/

section Over

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (U : Opens X.carrier)

/-- Transport generating sections from the open subspace `U` back to the slice site over `U`,
along the equivalence and an identification of the forward image. This is the analogue for
generating sections of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationOfOpenSubspaceIso`, and it has the same
two inputs: the inverse of the equivalence preserves colimits, being a left adjoint, and
`TopologicalSpace.Opens.sheafOfModulesEquivOverInverseUnit` says it takes the structure sheaf of
the open subspace to the structure sheaf of the slice site. The index type is unchanged. -/
noncomputable def generatingSectionsOfOpenSubspaceIso
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} ((structureSheafRing X).over U)}
    {N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing (openSubspace U))}
    (e : (openSubspaceEquiv U).functor.obj M ≅ N) (σ : N.GeneratingSections) :
    M.GeneratingSections :=
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso
      ((openSubspaceEquiv U).unitIso.app M ≪≫ (openSubspaceEquiv U).inverse.mapIso e)).symm
    (σ.map (openSubspaceEquiv U).inverse
      (U.sheafOfModulesEquivOverInverseUnit (structureSheafRing X)).symm)

variable (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))
  (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F)

/-- **Generating sections of `F` over an open give generating sections of every symmetric power of
`F` over that same open**, finitely many when the given ones are finitely many. As in
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_symmetricPower_over`, the uniformity in the degree
matters: one open serves every degree, with no further shrinking. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower_over
    (σ : (F.over U).GeneratingSections) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ τ : ((A.symmetricPower n).over U).GeneratingSections, (Finite σ.I → Finite τ.I) := by
  have hB := _root_.SheafOfModules.isSymmetricAlgebra_sectionwiseSymmetricAlgebra_val
    (J := (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) (Osharp := X.sheaf.over U) (F.over U)
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ := exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower
    (σ.map (openSubspaceEquiv U).functor
      (U.sheafOfModulesEquivOverUnit (structureSheafRing X)).symm)
    (openSubspaceAlgebras U F) n
  exact ⟨(_root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso
      (symmetricPowerOverIso F U n A.symmetric A.symmetricGenerator
        A.symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra _ _ hB).symm)
    (generatingSectionsOfOpenSubspaceIso U (symmetricPowerPushforwardIso
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) (openSubspaceSiteFunctor U)
      (Jt := (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) (Osharp := X.sheaf.over U)
      (F.over U) n _ _ hB (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).symmetric
      (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).symmetricGenerator
      (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).symmetric_isSymmetricAlgebra) τ), hτ⟩

/-- **Generating sections of `F` over an open give generating sections of every exterior power of
`F` over that same open**, finitely many when the given ones are finitely many. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower_over
    (σ : (F.over U).GeneratingSections) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ τ : ((A.exteriorPower n).over U).GeneratingSections, (Finite σ.I → Finite τ.I) := by
  have hB := _root_.SheafOfModules.isExteriorAlgebra_sectionwiseExteriorAlgebra_val
    (J := (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) (Osharp := X.sheaf.over U) (F.over U)
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ := exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower
    (σ.map (openSubspaceEquiv U).functor
      (U.sheafOfModulesEquivOverUnit (structureSheafRing X)).symm)
    (openSubspaceAlgebras U F) n
  exact ⟨(_root_.SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso
      (exteriorPowerOverIso F U n A.exterior A.exteriorGenerator
        A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra _ _ hB).symm)
    (generatingSectionsOfOpenSubspaceIso U (exteriorPowerPushforwardIso
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥U) (openSubspaceSiteFunctor U)
      (Jt := (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier).over U) (Osharp := X.sheaf.over U)
      (F.over U) n _ _ hB (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).exterior
      (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).exteriorGenerator
      (openSubspaceAlgebras U F).exterior_isExteriorAlgebra) τ), hτ⟩

end Over

/-! ### Clauses (1) and (2) of Tag 01CK for the symmetric and exterior powers -/

section Conclusions

variable {X : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing X))
  (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology X.carrier) F)

/-- The local generators of `Symⁿ F` built from local generators of `F`: the same covering, with
the generating sections produced in each member by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower_over`. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower
    (q : F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) (n : ℕ) :
    (A.symmetricPower n).LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u} where
  I := q.I
  X := q.X
  coversTop := q.coversTop
  generators := fun i =>
    (exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower_over (q.X i) F A (q.generators i) n).choose

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower` is of finite type when the given
local generators are. -/
instance localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower_isFiniteType
    (q : F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) (n : ℕ) [h : q.IsFiniteType] :
    (localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower F A q n).IsFiniteType where
  isFiniteType i :=
    have hfin : Finite (q.generators i).I := (h.isFiniteType i).finite
    ⟨(exists_generatingSections_symmetricPower_over (q.X i) F A
      (q.generators i) n).choose_spec hfin⟩

/-- The local generators of `⋀ⁿ F` built from local generators of `F`. -/
noncomputable def localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower
    (q : F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) (n : ℕ) :
    (A.exteriorPower n).LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u} where
  I := q.I
  X := q.X
  coversTop := q.coversTop
  generators := fun i =>
    (exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower_over (q.X i) F A (q.generators i) n).choose

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower` is of finite type when the given
local generators are. -/
instance localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower_isFiniteType
    (q : F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) (n : ℕ) [h : q.IsFiniteType] :
    (localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower F A q n).IsFiniteType where
  isFiniteType i :=
    have hfin : Finite (q.generators i).I := (h.isFiniteType i).finite
    ⟨(exists_generatingSections_exteriorPower_over (q.X i) F A
      (q.generators i) n).choose_spec hfin⟩

/-- **Each symmetric power of a sheaf of modules locally generated by sections on a ringed space
is locally generated by sections.** This is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 01CK] for the symmetric
powers. -/
@[stacks 01CK "symmetric powers of a module locally generated by sections"]
theorem nonempty_localGeneratorsData_symmetricPower
    (hF : Nonempty (F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u})) (n : ℕ) :
    Nonempty ((A.symmetricPower n).LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) :=
  ⟨localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower F A hF.some n⟩

/-- **Each exterior power of a sheaf of modules locally generated by sections on a ringed space is
locally generated by sections.** This is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 01CK] for the exterior
powers. -/
@[stacks 01CK "exterior powers of a module locally generated by sections"]
theorem nonempty_localGeneratorsData_exteriorPower
    (hF : Nonempty (F.LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u})) (n : ℕ) :
    Nonempty ((A.exteriorPower n).LocalGeneratorsData.{u, u, u, u}) :=
  ⟨localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower F A hF.some n⟩

/-- **Each symmetric power of a sheaf of modules of finite type on a ringed space is of finite
type.** This is clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 01CK] for the symmetric powers: the covering is the one
on which `F` is generated by finitely many sections, and the index type produced in degree `n` is
the set of degree-`n` multidegrees in the given one, hence finite. -/
@[stacks 01CK "symmetric powers of a module of finite type", ega "II 1.7.7" "more general"]
theorem isFiniteType_symmetricPower
    [hF : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F] (n : ℕ) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} (A.symmetricPower n) := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData F
  constructor
  exact ⟨localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower F A q n,
    localGeneratorsDataSymmetricPower_isFiniteType F A q n (h := hq)⟩

/-- **Each exterior power of a sheaf of modules of finite type on a ringed space is of finite
type.** This is clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 01CK] for the exterior powers. The primed name
distinguishes it from `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_exteriorPower`, which assumes `F` of
finite presentation and is therefore not this clause. -/
@[stacks 01CK "exterior powers of a module of finite type"]
theorem isFiniteType_exteriorPower'
    [hF : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F] (n : ℕ) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} (A.exteriorPower n) := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := _root_.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData F
  constructor
  exact ⟨localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower F A q n,
    localGeneratorsDataExteriorPower_isFiniteType F A q n (h := hq)⟩

end Conclusions

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
